1
00:00:01,208 --> 00:00:02,917
[mysterious music]

2
00:00:03,042 --> 00:00:06,042
It makes no sense that our
monastery is way out here.

3
00:00:06,167 --> 00:00:07,750
How is this even possible?

4
00:00:09,667 --> 00:00:13,167
Because this isn't
our monastery.

5
00:00:13,292 --> 00:00:14,792
Whoa.

6
00:00:14,917 --> 00:00:16,417
From the outside,
it looks exactly the same,

7
00:00:16,542 --> 00:00:19,042
but in here, pretty different.

8
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:22,125
For real. As if someone liked
your crumbly old monastery

9
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:26,417
so much they were like,
"I'll have my own, please."

10
00:00:26,542 --> 00:00:29,208
I mean, your nice monastery.

11
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:31,792
[Cole] If Mysterium
is a land of magic,

12
00:00:31,917 --> 00:00:33,792
could this be an
illusion or something?

13
00:00:33,917 --> 00:00:37,083
Scans confirm
its solid existence.

14
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:40,292
Bonzle, the Sorceress
created you here?

15
00:00:40,417 --> 00:00:42,250
I mean, in roughly this spot,

16
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:44,833
but there was
no building here then.

17
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:47,792
The Sorceress is
probably long gone,

18
00:00:47,917 --> 00:00:50,958
if she'd even remember
or recognize me.

19
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:52,917
After the Merge,

20
00:00:53,042 --> 00:00:56,125
I awoke inside a strange second
monastery under Imperium,

21
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:59,833
something I have not yet
been able to explain.

22
00:00:59,958 --> 00:01:02,500
And now, we have
a third monastery.

23
00:01:02,625 --> 00:01:04,583
Hmm, puzzling.

24
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:06,958
Both of you, come! Look!

25
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,750
[Bonzle] A crack
in the wall? So?

26
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:13,250
Long time ago,
back in our monastery,

27
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:15,542
my teammate Jay
and I got into a fight

28
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:18,083
because he was totally annoying
and I was completely blameless.

29
00:01:18,208 --> 00:01:19,708
[electricity surges]

30
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:21,542
-[gadget whooshes]
-[wall cracks]

31
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:24,167
Anyway, during the fight,
we broke the wall,

32
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:26,625
making a crack in the shape
of a bowl of noodles.

33
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:29,000
[Zane] Cole and Jay thought
it looked so delicious,

34
00:01:29,125 --> 00:01:31,000
they got hungry,
stopped the fight,

35
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:33,292
and went to Chen's
Noodle House together.

36
00:01:33,417 --> 00:01:35,708
That's the weirdest way to end
a fight I've ever heard.

37
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:39,500
The point is that's
the exact crack we made.

38
00:01:39,625 --> 00:01:41,500
But how could this monastery

39
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:44,542
have the same cracks in
the walls as our monastery?

40
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:46,458
I don't know, but
it's making me hungry.

41
00:01:46,583 --> 00:01:49,250
I wish that bonehead
Jay was around.

42
00:01:49,375 --> 00:01:51,542
Who knows where he
ended up after the Merge?

43
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:54,750
[Sprite whirring]

44
00:01:56,167 --> 00:01:58,042
You saw that too, right?

45
00:01:58,167 --> 00:02:00,250
We have witnessed similar
unexplained phenomena

46
00:02:00,375 --> 00:02:01,833
at our monastery.

47
00:02:01,958 --> 00:02:05,333
The post-Merge world
has so many mysteries.

48
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:07,583
If only someone would arrive

49
00:02:07,708 --> 00:02:10,333
and tell us everything
we need to know.

50
00:02:10,458 --> 00:02:14,083
Hi! Oh, you have no idea
how glad I am

51
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:16,083
to set eyes on you.

52
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:20,375
Sprite told me you
finally got here.

53
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:24,500
I am Gandalaria, the High
Sorceress of Mysterium,

54
00:02:24,625 --> 00:02:28,333
and I have awaited your coming
for quite some time.

55
00:02:28,458 --> 00:02:30,500
This will change everything!

56
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:32,333
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

57
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:33,875
♪ So much to see ♪

58
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,667
♪ Together we will rise ♪

59
00:02:36,792 --> 00:02:40,083
♪ We fight ♪

60
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:43,708
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

61
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:46,042
[explosion booms]

62
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:48,750
[intense music]

63
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:54,042
-[Arin grunting]
-[columns crumbling]

64
00:02:54,167 --> 00:02:56,375
[Arin] Ah!

65
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:59,167
[Arin pants, groans]

66
00:02:59,292 --> 00:03:01,417
All right! Yeah!

67
00:03:01,542 --> 00:03:04,417
Sorry, didn't mean
to sneak up on you, Arin.

68
00:03:04,542 --> 00:03:07,542
I'm just trying to practice
Spinjitzu on my own.

69
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:09,167
And you're doing great!

70
00:03:09,292 --> 00:03:10,875
Don't make fun of me, Sora.

71
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,542
You know I got demoted
down to First Fang.

72
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:15,375
I'm not making fun of you.

73
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,958
You plowed right through
those first two pillars.

74
00:03:18,083 --> 00:03:20,458
I was trying to go
through all three

75
00:03:20,583 --> 00:03:24,208
with a proper Spinjitzu
tornado, for once.

76
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:26,917
Your Spinjitzu's been
great since I met you.

77
00:03:27,042 --> 00:03:30,250
I mean, you can give Spinjitzu
to inanimate objects.

78
00:03:30,375 --> 00:03:31,750
No one can do that.

79
00:03:31,875 --> 00:03:33,958
I can barely do that.

80
00:03:34,083 --> 00:03:36,083
Stop being so hard on yourself.

81
00:03:36,208 --> 00:03:39,417
The Blood Moon is coming!
The whole world is at stake!

82
00:03:39,542 --> 00:03:41,042
We're the only ones
who can stop it,

83
00:03:41,167 --> 00:03:43,917
and I need to be getting
better at being a Ninja,

84
00:03:44,042 --> 00:03:45,833
but I'm not.

85
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:55,208
[calm music]

86
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:59,917
I came here alone because I
do not wish to be disturbed.

87
00:04:00,042 --> 00:04:01,667
Yeah, me too.

88
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:04,542
Sometimes all those other
Ninja can get on my nerves.

89
00:04:04,625 --> 00:04:07,417
I mean, Kai's friends
are all good people,

90
00:04:07,542 --> 00:04:10,375
but I'm not used to being
around humans all the time.

91
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,750
I was raised by dragons.
Did you know that?

92
00:04:12,875 --> 00:04:17,083
You may have mentioned it
once or 12 times.

93
00:04:17,208 --> 00:04:19,708
Yeah, so I fit in better
with you and Rontu

94
00:04:19,833 --> 00:04:21,583
than the Ninja, really.

95
00:04:21,708 --> 00:04:22,875
Mm-hmm.

96
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,958
My family used to
tell me stories.

97
00:04:25,083 --> 00:04:28,500
I'm sure they were made up,
but they were very good.

98
00:04:28,625 --> 00:04:31,208
Some were about the two
greatest dragon warriors

99
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:34,208
-that ever lived.
-Is that so?

100
00:04:34,333 --> 00:04:38,042
Yeah, these warriors were epic.
Legendary.

101
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:39,875
They went to all the realms,

102
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,375
protecting everyone who
couldn't protect themselves

103
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,542
whether they were
dragons or not.

104
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:47,125
And the older dragon
was the bravest warrior

105
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:49,125
anyone had ever seen.

106
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:52,250
Hmm, was he, now?

107
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:55,917
Yep. We even named the largest
strongest mountain in our land

108
00:04:56,042 --> 00:04:58,667
after him: Mount Egalt.

109
00:04:58,792 --> 00:05:02,833
But those stories were
probably all just fairy tales.

110
00:05:02,958 --> 00:05:07,500
There was a time when those
stories could have been true,

111
00:05:07,625 --> 00:05:09,917
but that is long past.

112
00:05:10,042 --> 00:05:13,708
Time runs out for everyone,

113
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:16,250
even once-great warriors.

114
00:05:17,417 --> 00:05:20,875
I made you a stew from
Janus Melons and Xoa Thorns.

115
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,083
It helps ease the pain
of the Wasting Sickness.

116
00:05:24,208 --> 00:05:26,750
[grunts] What are you
talking about?

117
00:05:26,875 --> 00:05:29,917
I lost some of my
own dragon family to it.

118
00:05:30,042 --> 00:05:32,542
I know it's a disease
older dragons can get.

119
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:37,417
And what makes you believe
I suffer from this ailment?

120
00:05:37,542 --> 00:05:40,625
The black edges
of your lost scales.

121
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:44,750
That only happens when the
sickness is getting really bad.

122
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:48,583
This isn't a cure, but it
makes the pain less painful.

123
00:05:48,708 --> 00:05:53,417
I don't need any stew.
I just need to be left alone.

124
00:05:53,542 --> 00:05:55,042
Irritability is
one of the symptoms

125
00:05:55,167 --> 00:05:57,333
of Wasting Sickness too,

126
00:05:57,458 --> 00:06:00,417
but that could also just
be your personality.

127
00:06:00,542 --> 00:06:01,542
Ha!

128
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:08,167
So, they named
a mountain after me, huh?

129
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,875
Now, pay attention.
This is very important.

130
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,917
I'll need 20 striped ones,

131
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:21,125
five red betties,
and two extra-slimy.

132
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:24,583
I am sorry.
We do not understand.

133
00:06:24,708 --> 00:06:26,000
What?
What's not to understand?

134
00:06:26,125 --> 00:06:28,417
Oh, and do you have
any with wings?

135
00:06:28,542 --> 00:06:31,167
I could really use
some with wings.

136
00:06:31,292 --> 00:06:33,708
Some whats with wings?

137
00:06:33,833 --> 00:06:35,542
Slugs, of course.

138
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:37,875
Aren't you
the traveling slug merchants

139
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,833
I've been waiting for?

140
00:06:39,958 --> 00:06:41,625
Slug merchants?

141
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,708
But you said our arrival
would change everything.

142
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:46,333
Uh, yeah!

143
00:06:46,458 --> 00:06:49,208
I've been very low on
rare magic ingredients

144
00:06:49,333 --> 00:06:52,375
for, like, weeks now, and
a really good set of slugs

145
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,917
would change all that.

146
00:06:55,042 --> 00:06:56,375
Slugs are pretty cool,
actually.

147
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:59,875
Perhaps, yet we
have none to sell.

148
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,292
Ah, bummer. Well, what
am I going to do now?

149
00:07:04,417 --> 00:07:07,583
Would you all mind if
I turn you into slugs?

150
00:07:07,708 --> 00:07:09,792
We would mind that
very, very much.

151
00:07:09,917 --> 00:07:11,542
Are you sure?

152
00:07:11,667 --> 00:07:14,792
Because you'd make
really groovy slugs,

153
00:07:14,917 --> 00:07:17,000
I can tell
just by looking at...

154
00:07:17,125 --> 00:07:20,042
[gasps] It's you!

155
00:07:20,167 --> 00:07:23,917
My dearest!
You've come home!

156
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:29,250
You... You recognize me?
Even in my boney physical form?

157
00:07:29,375 --> 00:07:33,958
Oh, I would know
your true essence anywhere.

158
00:07:34,083 --> 00:07:37,500
I was so afraid you wouldn't
accept me for who I am now.

159
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:39,125
Are you kidding?

160
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:43,250
I put my heart, my soul
into every spell I weave.

161
00:07:43,375 --> 00:07:47,333
And even though spells
usually fade away after use,

162
00:07:47,458 --> 00:07:50,125
I always hoped you
would be different--

163
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:54,083
the most complex spell
I've ever woven,

164
00:07:54,208 --> 00:07:58,542
and the first of my creations
to ever come back to me!

165
00:07:58,667 --> 00:08:00,333
Oh!

166
00:08:03,833 --> 00:08:05,083
[Lloyd sips]

167
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:06,917
[sighs]

168
00:08:08,542 --> 00:08:10,292
[Rontu sips, gulps]

169
00:08:10,417 --> 00:08:13,042
So you're afraid these
visions are holding you back

170
00:08:13,167 --> 00:08:15,958
from progressing with
your Rising Dragon training?

171
00:08:16,083 --> 00:08:20,625
I'm just a bundle of nerves,
stumbling around in a daze.

172
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:24,250
I'm even afraid to rest because
more visions might come.

173
00:08:24,375 --> 00:08:25,875
Why would that be a bad thing?

174
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,917
Because they're terrifying!
I see evil things.

175
00:08:30,042 --> 00:08:33,000
My friends in danger,
it's awful.

176
00:08:33,125 --> 00:08:34,750
I'm sure it is,

177
00:08:34,875 --> 00:08:37,583
but these visions are also
important warnings, right?

178
00:08:37,708 --> 00:08:39,208
[sighs]

179
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:42,583
They are, but they're
also tearing me apart.

180
00:08:42,708 --> 00:08:46,500
Master Wu taught that when
there is no calm outside of you,

181
00:08:46,625 --> 00:08:49,917
you must find the calm inside,

182
00:08:50,042 --> 00:08:52,833
but I have no calm
inside of me anymore.

183
00:08:52,958 --> 00:08:55,708
You held the power
of a Source Dragon,

184
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:58,667
something no mortal
was ever meant to do.

185
00:08:58,792 --> 00:09:01,500
These possible futures
are after-effects.

186
00:09:01,625 --> 00:09:03,333
Possible futures?

187
00:09:03,458 --> 00:09:06,042
Source Dragons experience
time differently

188
00:09:06,167 --> 00:09:07,375
than the rest of us.

189
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,833
They can see what came before

190
00:09:08,958 --> 00:09:11,333
and the things that
might come to be.

191
00:09:11,458 --> 00:09:14,875
These visions you're having
are like a fragment of that.

192
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,542
But how can I stop them?

193
00:09:16,667 --> 00:09:18,167
You can't.

194
00:09:18,292 --> 00:09:20,000
You can never force
the motion of the universe

195
00:09:20,125 --> 00:09:21,833
to bend to your will,

196
00:09:21,958 --> 00:09:24,583
you can only find your
place within its current.

197
00:09:24,708 --> 00:09:26,375
But with careful meditation,

198
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:29,458
it's possible you can find
harmony with these visions

199
00:09:29,583 --> 00:09:32,417
so you no longer have
to live in fear of them.

200
00:09:32,542 --> 00:09:34,375
No. I need to stop them.

201
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,333
Because when they come on,
I can't-- [shouts]

202
00:09:37,458 --> 00:09:39,917
[eerie music]

203
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,917
But that will kill him!

204
00:09:47,042 --> 00:09:50,708
[weapons clanging]

205
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:54,792
[explosion booms]

206
00:09:54,917 --> 00:09:57,375
[yells]
The Blood Moon!

207
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,792
It's so close!
It's almost here!

208
00:10:00,917 --> 00:10:04,208
Unless we stop him, Lord Ras
is going to sacrifice someone,

209
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:06,083
and Cole and Zane are doomed!

210
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:07,542
Then time is of the essence.

211
00:10:07,667 --> 00:10:09,667
Return to training immediately.

212
00:10:09,792 --> 00:10:12,417
If you cannot learn
Rising Dragon Technique,

213
00:10:12,542 --> 00:10:14,750
all will be lost.

214
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:17,625
[calm music]

215
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,167
Ahem, uh, Sorceress?

216
00:10:20,292 --> 00:10:22,625
Please, call me Gandalaria.

217
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:23,625
Of course.

218
00:10:23,792 --> 00:10:27,500
Gadull-- Gandollar, uh...

219
00:10:27,583 --> 00:10:31,167
Sorceress, we came because
we gotta protect Bonzle.

220
00:10:31,292 --> 00:10:33,083
Scary Wolf Mask
people are after her

221
00:10:33,208 --> 00:10:34,542
so their Lord Ras can use her

222
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:37,167
to unleash evil
on the Merged lands.

223
00:10:37,292 --> 00:10:39,583
Okay, now I might've been
getting a little slow

224
00:10:39,708 --> 00:10:42,208
on the uptake for the last
couple of hundred years,

225
00:10:42,333 --> 00:10:46,375
but what's a Bonzle,
or a Lord Ras?

226
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,917
I'm Bonzle. That's the name
I chose when I became a person.

227
00:10:50,042 --> 00:10:54,042
Well, that's a splendid name.

228
00:10:54,167 --> 00:10:57,500
Lord Ras is a villain
we Ninja have faced before.

229
00:10:57,625 --> 00:11:00,500
He is determined
to free the Forbidden Five.

230
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:04,208
The foes I created
Bonzle to banish?

231
00:11:04,333 --> 00:11:06,708
-Exactly.
-Ah, pfft, then no problem.

232
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:09,833
They're gone, exiled,
never able to return.

233
00:11:09,958 --> 00:11:11,708
-You're certain?
-Of course.

234
00:11:11,833 --> 00:11:14,292
First off, it'd take
a whole complicated ritual

235
00:11:14,417 --> 00:11:16,292
that no one remembers how to
do,

236
00:11:16,417 --> 00:11:19,125
and second, it could only
be done under a Blood Moon,

237
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:22,708
and those happen like
once a millennium.

238
00:11:22,833 --> 00:11:25,500
It appears we have bad news.

239
00:11:25,625 --> 00:11:29,042
The details of the ritual
were recovered by Lord Ras

240
00:11:29,167 --> 00:11:31,583
from the Cloud Kingdom
archives.

241
00:11:31,708 --> 00:11:35,083
And the Blood Moon
is coming soon.

242
00:11:35,208 --> 00:11:37,917
Oh. Oh!

243
00:11:38,042 --> 00:11:40,375
Yes, that does change things.

244
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,500
If this Ras times it right,

245
00:11:42,625 --> 00:11:44,583
reversing
the power of the spell--

246
00:11:44,708 --> 00:11:46,625
uh, Bonzle here--

247
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:50,375
I suppose he could
very well free the Five.

248
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,208
And from what we understand,

249
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:55,250
if they get loose, they
could conquer everything.

250
00:11:55,375 --> 00:11:58,708
Conquer?
More like obliterate!

251
00:11:58,833 --> 00:12:01,292
You musn't allow
them to be freed!

252
00:12:01,417 --> 00:12:02,875
We hoped you would know a way

253
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,458
to keep Bonzle safely
out of Ras' hands

254
00:12:05,583 --> 00:12:08,000
until the Blood Moon passes.

255
00:12:08,125 --> 00:12:09,625
Before I moved
into this new place,

256
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:11,708
I used to wander the lands.

257
00:12:11,833 --> 00:12:15,333
I keep most of
my materials in storage.

258
00:12:15,458 --> 00:12:17,625
So you have nothing
to help us with?

259
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:21,250
Well, not here, but I
certainly do in my storehouse.

260
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:23,417
It's in a land
called the Wyldness.

261
00:12:23,542 --> 00:12:26,292
It'll be quite
a journey on foot.

262
00:12:26,417 --> 00:12:27,958
Good news. We've got
our fastest dragon

263
00:12:28,083 --> 00:12:29,583
parked right outside.

264
00:12:29,708 --> 00:12:31,792
Ooh, how delightful!

265
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:35,417
I haven't ridden
on dragonback for a century!

266
00:12:35,542 --> 00:12:37,417
[gate thudding]

267
00:12:37,542 --> 00:12:39,667
[Cole] Did the Wolf Masks
follow us here?

268
00:12:39,792 --> 00:12:41,667
I do not believe
they would knock.

269
00:12:41,792 --> 00:12:45,000
However, it would be wise
to discover who is outside

270
00:12:45,125 --> 00:12:47,333
before we open that gate.

271
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:52,583
If it's a snail merchant,
ask about the ones with wings!

272
00:12:52,708 --> 00:12:55,375
Unfortunately, it is not.

273
00:12:57,917 --> 00:12:59,500
Attention!

274
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:03,917
My name is Agent Roderick
Allen, and this is my partner,

275
00:13:03,917 --> 00:13:06,375
Agent Underwood.

276
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:09,958
By the all-encompassing
authority of The Administration,

277
00:13:10,083 --> 00:13:13,542
we hereby demand
you open this door!

278
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:16,667
We're after the stolen
equipment known as Zane,

279
00:13:16,792 --> 00:13:19,833
who illegally fled from us!

280
00:13:19,958 --> 00:13:22,333
Cole, have I mentioned
that I was briefly kidnapped

281
00:13:22,458 --> 00:13:24,583
by a society of bureaucrats
from the Land of Madness

282
00:13:24,708 --> 00:13:26,625
who forced me to work
in their mail room,

283
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:28,458
where I introduced
efficiencies that raised

284
00:13:28,583 --> 00:13:31,292
delivery accuracy by nearly 9%?

285
00:13:31,417 --> 00:13:32,958
Are you serious?

286
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:34,708
Yes, nearly 9%.

287
00:13:34,833 --> 00:13:36,708
I feel I could have
gotten it to ten,

288
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:39,625
but Lloyd and Arin rescued me
before I could finish.

289
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:41,417
Bureaucrats? Pfft!

290
00:13:41,542 --> 00:13:44,167
Probably wouldn't even
make good slugs then.

291
00:13:44,292 --> 00:13:49,750
-[intense music]
-[Kai's Spinjitzu whirring]

292
00:13:51,083 --> 00:13:53,458
[Kai yelps]

293
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:55,417
[groans] Come on!

294
00:13:55,542 --> 00:13:58,875
This is impossible!
It's too much!

295
00:13:59,458 --> 00:14:02,333
Did I not tell you
it would be impossible?

296
00:14:02,458 --> 00:14:06,458
Rising Dragon Technique is not
for those lacking in spirit.

297
00:14:06,583 --> 00:14:09,083
Who are you saying
lacks spirit? Me?

298
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:11,083
You better not be
talking about me.

299
00:14:11,208 --> 00:14:12,958
So quick to anger.

300
00:14:13,083 --> 00:14:15,417
It is no surprise
you cannot find harmony

301
00:14:15,542 --> 00:14:17,583
with the universe's motion.

302
00:14:17,708 --> 00:14:20,375
What if we did
this drill together?

303
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,542
What?

304
00:14:21,667 --> 00:14:23,375
You say Rising Dragon Technique

305
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:26,167
is about finding
harmony with everything,

306
00:14:26,292 --> 00:14:29,292
which means harmony
with each other, right?

307
00:14:29,417 --> 00:14:30,833
It does.

308
00:14:30,958 --> 00:14:33,292
Then, let my brother
and I try this together.

309
00:14:33,417 --> 00:14:35,917
That is unprecedented,

310
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:39,375
but I don't have
a problem with it.

311
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,833
Though it will most
likely end in failure.

312
00:14:42,958 --> 00:14:45,292
What are you doing?
I can do this myself, Nya.

313
00:14:45,417 --> 00:14:47,667
So far, you're doing
better than any of us,

314
00:14:47,792 --> 00:14:50,250
but I know what's
holding you back.

315
00:14:50,375 --> 00:14:53,708
-What?
-You. Stop thinking about you.

316
00:14:53,833 --> 00:14:56,458
Start thinking
about Counter Shot.

317
00:14:56,583 --> 00:14:58,667
The game we made up
in Dad's blacksmith shop?

318
00:14:58,792 --> 00:15:01,958
[chuckles]
Wow, miss those days.

319
00:15:02,083 --> 00:15:05,958
Just fun, not having to worry
about saving the world.

320
00:15:06,083 --> 00:15:08,083
And who was your best
Counter Shot partner?

321
00:15:08,208 --> 00:15:09,208
[Egalt] Begin!

322
00:15:09,333 --> 00:15:10,625
[Spinjitzus whirring]

323
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:13,333
[epic music]

324
00:15:18,708 --> 00:15:20,125
[epic music continues]

325
00:15:26,042 --> 00:15:26,917
[Kai whooshes]

326
00:15:27,042 --> 00:15:28,375
[horseshoes clang]

327
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,417
-[Spinjitzus whirring]
-[targets clang]

328
00:15:30,542 --> 00:15:32,875
[epic music builds]

329
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,500
[horseshoes whooshing]

330
00:15:36,375 --> 00:15:38,375
-[epic music continues]
-[pots breaking]

331
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,458
[boulders breaking]

332
00:15:40,583 --> 00:15:44,167
[epic music continues]

333
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:50,583
[dragon roaring]

334
00:15:50,708 --> 00:15:55,833
-[epic music building]
-[dragon whooshing]

335
00:16:00,375 --> 00:16:02,167
[epic music climaxes
then fades out]

336
00:16:02,292 --> 00:16:05,542
-[dragon roars]
-[explosion booms]

337
00:16:05,667 --> 00:16:08,417
[gasps]
I did it! I did it!

338
00:16:08,542 --> 00:16:10,583
Nya, thank you so much!

339
00:16:10,708 --> 00:16:12,000
Ohh, you were so right!

340
00:16:12,125 --> 00:16:15,042
[all cheering]

341
00:16:17,458 --> 00:16:22,625
Kai is now officially
a Third Fang Ninja.

342
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:25,708
When you first arrived,
I was skeptical.

343
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:29,750
But I had become old and tired,
without inspiration,

344
00:16:29,875 --> 00:16:32,833
and it was clear
I misjudged you.

345
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:35,333
You are worthy students

346
00:16:35,458 --> 00:16:38,833
and have given this old dragon
the spark of hope

347
00:16:38,958 --> 00:16:42,583
that Rising Dragon
Technique will be passed on.

348
00:16:42,708 --> 00:16:44,625
What's wrong with the sky?

349
00:16:46,708 --> 00:16:48,042
Oh, no.

350
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:50,750
[ominous music]

351
00:16:50,875 --> 00:16:54,042
[dramatic music]

352
00:17:05,708 --> 00:17:07,292
The Blood Moon is here.

353
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,083
Come on!
We have no time to waste.

354
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:15,250
Help the rest of us learn how
to do Rising Dragon Technique.

355
00:17:15,375 --> 00:17:17,958
We cannot. I'm sorry.

356
00:17:18,083 --> 00:17:19,750
We hoped we had more time,

357
00:17:19,875 --> 00:17:22,917
but the Blood Moon
is also a bane for us.

358
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,792
May the Source Dragons
be on your side.

359
00:17:29,125 --> 00:17:32,875
[dramatic music continues]

360
00:17:44,417 --> 00:17:48,583
Excuse me. We have some rather
pressing matters to attend to.

361
00:17:48,708 --> 00:17:50,208
Would it be easiest
for my allies here

362
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:51,958
if I just surrendered?

363
00:17:52,083 --> 00:17:55,333
Technically, you can't
surrender, only people can.

364
00:17:55,458 --> 00:17:57,042
You're a robotic Nindroid,

365
00:17:57,167 --> 00:18:00,208
so you're classified
as equipment, not personnel.

366
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:03,042
Which means you'll
be decommissioned

367
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:05,208
in our incinerator.

368
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:06,875
But that will kill him!

369
00:18:07,083 --> 00:18:10,583
Correction, it would kill
him, if he were a person.

370
00:18:10,625 --> 00:18:13,917
But he's just equipment,
so no big deal.

371
00:18:14,042 --> 00:18:17,708
But if I turn myself over,
my friends can go free?

372
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:21,000
Nope. Don't you
know Addendum 47-A?

373
00:18:21,125 --> 00:18:23,167
Anyone assisting
a known fugitive

374
00:18:23,292 --> 00:18:26,458
shall be punished under
the strictest guidelines.

375
00:18:26,583 --> 00:18:29,750
Not much room for
misinterpretation there.

376
00:18:29,875 --> 00:18:32,500
Whatever. Let's just get on
our dragon and go, everyone.

377
00:18:32,625 --> 00:18:37,250
Nice try, but your dragon's
currently impounded.

378
00:18:38,958 --> 00:18:41,292
[Jiro roars]

379
00:18:41,417 --> 00:18:44,042
[Cole] Hey! Let Jiro go!

380
00:18:44,167 --> 00:18:47,625
We can discuss it on the way
to the incinerator.

381
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:49,333
Breach this wall!

382
00:18:49,458 --> 00:18:50,500
Halt!

383
00:18:50,625 --> 00:18:53,167
Where is your 35-C91 form,

384
00:18:53,292 --> 00:18:55,417
designating approved
intent to breach a wall

385
00:18:55,542 --> 00:18:57,708
or barricade on foreign soil?

386
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,500
Did you just make that up?

387
00:19:00,625 --> 00:19:02,542
No. My work in the mail room
afforded me

388
00:19:02,667 --> 00:19:04,458
much access to handbooks.

389
00:19:04,583 --> 00:19:07,417
My knowledge
of their regulations is vast.

390
00:19:07,542 --> 00:19:12,042
[groans] Intent to breach
water. Intent to breach
walrus.

391
00:19:12,167 --> 00:19:15,792
Ah, here it is!
Intent to breach walls.

392
00:19:15,917 --> 00:19:19,500
Ugh, he's right.
We need forms!

393
00:19:19,625 --> 00:19:21,500
[groans]
Okay, give us a minute.

394
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:23,583
We'll get right
on the paperwork.

395
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,208
Man, none of this stuff
is Administration-approved,

396
00:19:31,333 --> 00:19:33,042
and you brought them
right to my door!

397
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:36,000
-[cat yowls]
-Not cool!

398
00:19:36,125 --> 00:19:39,042
We passed through
the Land of Madness to get here.

399
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:42,417
I should have realized
they would be scanning for me.

400
00:19:42,542 --> 00:19:44,292
This is all my fault.

401
00:19:44,417 --> 00:19:47,417
No. We're in this together.

402
00:19:47,542 --> 00:19:52,125
[Agent Underwood]
There's your 35-C91! Hmm!

403
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:56,375
This doesn't have
the mandatory 5-21z appendix.

404
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:57,750
Unacceptable.

405
00:19:59,333 --> 00:20:01,250
[Agent Allen]
Ugh, he's right again!

406
00:20:01,375 --> 00:20:03,250
Who's got a copy
of the appendix?

407
00:20:03,375 --> 00:20:08,667
I know what to do! I'll weave
an intricate escape spell.

408
00:20:08,792 --> 00:20:09,792
How long will that take?

409
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:12,667
Only two to three days.

410
00:20:12,792 --> 00:20:15,500
That might be too long.

411
00:20:16,583 --> 00:20:20,625
[Agent Allen] Appendix
attached, you scofflaw.

412
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:22,542
This is done correctly...

413
00:20:22,667 --> 00:20:26,208
-Told you.
-...but not in triplicate.

414
00:20:26,333 --> 00:20:28,625
-[Agent Allan screams]
-[gate thuds]

415
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:31,000
Bonzle, hide in the passages
under this place.

416
00:20:31,125 --> 00:20:33,417
Sprite will guide you.

417
00:20:33,542 --> 00:20:35,958
Thanks, Sprite.
But what are you gonna do?

418
00:20:36,083 --> 00:20:40,125
I'm going to fire up
my crystal ball!

419
00:20:41,125 --> 00:20:43,458
I'm not sure offering to read
their fortune is gonna help.

420
00:20:43,583 --> 00:20:46,417
It's not that kind
of crystal ball.

421
00:20:46,542 --> 00:20:51,208
-[ominous music]
-[gate crumbles]

422
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:54,542
There's your
triplicate right there!

423
00:20:56,500 --> 00:21:00,583
[blasts blaring]

424
00:21:00,708 --> 00:21:03,000
-[crystal ball surging]
-[Sorceress laughing]

425
00:21:03,125 --> 00:21:06,167
-[intense music]
-[mech assembling]

426
00:21:12,458 --> 00:21:14,500
[mechs clanging]

427
00:21:14,625 --> 00:21:16,917
[blasts blaring
and connecting]

428
00:21:17,042 --> 00:21:20,875
-[crystal ball surging]
-[Sorceress cackling]

429
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:25,792
[sighs] Everything's so dark
down here, Sprite.

430
00:21:25,917 --> 00:21:28,792
Are you sure there'll
be a safe place to hide?

431
00:21:28,917 --> 00:21:31,583
-[blast lands]
-[Agent Walker] Attention!

432
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:34,583
[mysterious music]

433
00:21:34,708 --> 00:21:36,500
My name
is Agent Jay Walker!

434
00:21:36,625 --> 00:21:40,083
By the all-encompassing
authority of the Administration,

435
00:21:40,208 --> 00:21:42,625
I hereby demand your surrender!

436
00:21:42,750 --> 00:21:44,875
[dramatic music]

437
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,042
[closing theme music playing]

